      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "To assess the influence of low dose rofecoxib on inflammatory mediators and prostacyclin synthesis in patients with acute coronary syndromes (ACS) in a short-term follow up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "Twenty nine patients with ACS without ST elevation were randomized to simvastatin alone or together with low dose rofecoxib. Serum levels of interleukin 6 (IL-6), 6-keto-PGF-1alpha--stable product of prostacyclin (PGT2) and hs-C-reactive protein (hs-CRP) were assessed on enrollment and after 30-day follow up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Combination of rofecoxib with statin significantly decreased levels of hs-CRP after one month therapy (5.21 mg/l +/- 4.12 vs 2.11 mg/l +/- 2.1; p=0.0092). This effect was not evident in a group on statin alone (3.95 mg/l +/- 3.33 vs 2.48 mg/l +/- 2.39; p=0.31). 6-keto-PGF-1alpha increased not significantly in both groups. IL-6 concentration has not changed during follow up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Low dose of selective COX-2 inhibitor exerts significant anti-inflammatory effect and does not diminish PG12 synthesis in study group of patients with ACS."
        }
      ]},
